      "verification_note": "Form 40 booklet 2024 (24f40bk.pdf) standard-deduction chart page 9: maximum $3,000 single / $8,500 joint (AGI phase-down not modeled). Line 13 personal exemption $1,500 single / $3,000 joint. Federal income tax deduction worksheet and dependent-exemption chart are not modeled. 2022 Form 40 What's New cites Acts 2022-292 and 2022-297 for the current standard-deduction chart. Tax years 2019-2021: NBER TAXSIM archive copies of the ADOR Form 40 booklets (standard-deduction chart page 9 maximum $2,500 single / $7,500 joint; page 6 personal exemption $1,500 single / $3,000 joint). Tax year 2018: NBER TAXSIM archive copy of the ADOR Form 40 (2-page form; page 1 Filing Status/Exemptions $1,500 single / $3,000 joint; standard-deduction chart not in that file). ADOR individual income tax filing information (https://www.revenue.alabama.gov/individual-corporate/individual-income-tax-filing-information/, sha256 7f883430000830825690ac25e468a3762731ae1c15c26b85bcdc775a3c421f52, retrieved 2026-11-10) states the brackets (2% on the first $500 single or $1,000 joint, 4% on the next $2,500 single or $5,000 joint, 5% over $3,000 single or $6,000 joint) and a personal exemption of $1,500 single / $3,000 joint. It does not state the standard-deduction amounts.",
